window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-4be553900db6f494"]={"key":"ny_b1-4be553900db6f494","group":"ny_b1","uid":"4be553900db6f494","rank":43,"title":"merrowdale cross holding obligor exposure","occupation":"financial_investment_analysts","archetype":"code_exec","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Noor Gallagher, the financial analyst responsible for Merrowdale Public Finance's annual credit refresh, and Arjun Voskresensky needs the concentration written clearly enough for the credit committee to use without a separate walkthrough. Merrowdale holds lease-backed certificates from eleven school districts across three states that were approved separately over four years; the supplied `certificate_holdings.json` is the complete source for this review. Build `cross_holding_obligor_memo.zip` in the top level of the working directory, containing `cross_holding_obligor_memo.py` and `README.md`. The Python 3.11 package must expose `build_memo(source, as_of, materiality_pct=0.10)`, where `source` is the parsed object from that JSON file, `as_of` is an ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` string, and `materiality_pct` is a number in the open-to-zero, closed-at-one interval. It must return a JSON-serializable dictionary with `as_of`, `total_prior_exposure`, `total_current_exposure`, `total_change`, `obligors`, `material_changes`, `concentration`, and `recommendation`. Each source certificate has a unique `certificate_id`, `issuer`, `state`, non-negative numeric `prior_exposure` and `current_exposure`, `appropriation_text`, and `operator_disclosure`; reject a source that is not an object with a `certificates` list, has duplicate IDs, missing fields, non-string text fields, non-finite or negative exposures, or an empty certificate list by raising `ValueError`, and reject an `as_of` value that is not a real ISO date or a `materiality_pct` of zero, a negative number, or a number above one with `ValueError`. Group certificates by the case-insensitive, whitespace-normalized operator disclosure, not by issuer. Confirm a linkage only when that normalized disclosure is also present in the corresponding appropriation text; retain the issuer-level rows and both source texts as evidence. For every operator report prior exposure, current exposure, change, current share of the portfolio, certificate count, and certificate IDs in deterministic order. Mark a change material when its absolute value is at least `materiality_pct` times prior exposure, except that a zero prior exposure is material only when current exposure is non-zero. Report the largest confirmed operator concentration and recommend heightened committee review when its current share is at least 0.30; otherwise recommend routine monitoring. Sort all emitted lists deterministically, use decimal-safe arithmetic or an equivalent approach that avoids unstable binary rounding, and make repeated runs on the same input identical. The README should document the contract, validation behavior, linkage evidence, assumptions, and an offline reproduction example.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/certificate_holdings.json` — Complete synthetic source for the eleven lease-backed certificates, including prior and current exposures, issuer and state fields, appropriation language, and appendix operator disclosures.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `cross_holding_obligor_memo.zip` — Offline Python 3.11 analytical model and maintainer documentation for producing the cross-holding obligor exposure memo. (The archive must contain cross_holding_obligor_memo.py and README.md.; The Python module must be executable and importable without network access or non-standard dependencies.; The documented public entry point and returned object must match the request exactly.; The implementation must not depend on wall-clock time, unseeded randomness, or hidden external data.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/certificate_holdings.json","bytes":3811,"extension":".json","url":"assets/0d5777a666d7e16e88456b503d0bbf8574c8befdb8dfbe2089fe5088f0945bf7.json","sha256":"0d5777a666d7e16e88456b503d0bbf8574c8befdb8dfbe2089fe5088f0945bf7","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"{\n  \"certificates\": [\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"MD-001\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Merrowdale Unified School District\",\n      \"state\": \"MD\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 900000,\n      \"current_exposure\": 1100000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"Annual appropriation payable to Foxglove Clinic under the lease support agreement.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \"Foxglove Clinic\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"OR-014\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Orchard Ridge Schools\",\n      \"state\": \"OR\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 1000000,\n      \"current_exposure\": 1050000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"The district will appropriate amounts due to FOXGLOVE CLINIC for facility operations.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \" foxglove   clinic \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"PA-207\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Pinehaven Area School Authority\",\n      \"state\": \"PA\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 800000,\n      \"current_exposure\": 900000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"Lease payments to Foxglove Clinic are included in the annual budget resolution.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \"FOXGLOVE CLINIC\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"MD-118\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Quarryfield County Schools\",\n      \"state\": \"MD\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 700000,\n      \"current_exposure\": 850000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"Quarryfield County Schools shall remit lease-backed certificate payments to Foxglove Clinic.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \"Foxglove Clinic\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"OR-091\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Silver Brook Education District\",\n      \"state\": \"OR\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 950000,\n      \"current_exposure\": 1300000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"Budgeted rent and service payments identify Foxglove Clinic as the facility operator.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \"Foxglove   Clinic\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"PA-033\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Cedar Vale School District\",\n      \"state\": \"PA\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 600000,\n      \"current_exposure\": 650000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"Cedar Vale appropriates lease payments to Northstar Learning Services.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \"Northstar Learning Services\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"MD-044\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Lake Juniper Schools\",\n      \"state\": \"MD\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 500000,\n      \"current_exposure\": 450000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"The appropriation covers the scheduled lease payment to Northstar Learning Services.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \"Northstar Learning Services\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"OR-155\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Quarryfield School District\",\n      \"state\": \"OR\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 450000,\n      \"current_exposure\": 400000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"Lease-backed certificates are payable to Harborline Operations.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \"Harborline Operations\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"PA-088\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Westmere Borough Schools\",\n      \"state\": \"PA\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 400000,\n      \"current_exposure\": 500000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"Westmere's annual resolution provides for payments to Harborline Operations.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \"Harborline Operations\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"MD-176\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Eastbank Public Schools\",\n      \"state\": \"MD\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 300000,\n      \"current_exposure\": 350000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"The district's lease schedule names Meridian Campus Partners.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \"Meridian Campus Partners\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"certificate_id\": \"OR-203\",\n      \"issuer\": \"Quarryfield Energy Schools Consortium\",\n      \"state\": \"OR\",\n      \"prior_exposure\": 0,\n      \"current_exposure\": 250000,\n      \"appropriation_text\": \"The 2026 appropriation reserves funds for a future facilities operator pending award.\",\n      \"operator_disclosure\": \"Meridian Campus Partners\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","truncated":false}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/cross_holding_obligor_memo.zip","bytes":3736,"extension":".zip","url":"assets/5a50635aaee851d6c1162dd692514e9d684ca1ba0abd3982fefba093a2c06bd1.zip","sha256":"5a50635aaee851d6c1162dd692514e9d684ca1ba0abd3982fefba093a2c06bd1","preview":{"kind":"unavailable","note":"此格式未做网页解析，原文件可下载。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A valid source with eleven certificates produces a JSON-serializable dictionary containing all eight required top-level result fields.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Execute the public entry point and serialize its return value with json.dumps.","grader_hint":"Use the supplied source and a valid as_of date; verify the required keys and successful serialization."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Prior exposure, current exposure, and total change are aggregated from all certificates without dropping or duplicating a certificate.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compare returned totals with independently summed source values.","grader_hint":"Use Decimal or a tolerance of ±0.01 monetary units for comparison."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Certificates are grouped by normalized operator disclosure rather than issuer, so the five certificates sharing the same disclosed operator form one obligor group.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Inspect obligor groups and certificate IDs.","grader_hint":"Confirm the five linked records are together even though their issuer values differ."},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Operator normalization is case-insensitive and collapses repeated whitespace while preserving the underlying evidence texts.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Run a fixture with case and whitespace variants and inspect grouping and retained texts.","grader_hint":"Variants that normalize to the same name must not create separate obligors."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A linkage is confirmed only when the normalized operator disclosure occurs in the corresponding appropriation text; issuer similarity or a common template alone does not confirm it.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Run positive and negative linkage fixtures.","grader_hint":"A record whose disclosure is absent from appropriation text must not be counted in confirmed concentration."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each issuer-level evidence row retains the issuer, certificate ID, appropriation text, and operator disclosure needed to substantiate the linkage.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Inspect returned obligor evidence.","grader_hint":"Do not accept a result that reports only a group name and totals."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each obligor reports prior exposure, current exposure, change, current portfolio share, certificate count, and certificate IDs.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Inspect every obligor object.","grader_hint":"Recompute each numeric field from the source and allow ±0.01 for monetary values and ±0.0001 for shares."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Current portfolio share equals current obligor exposure divided by total current exposure, with a zero-total portfolio handled without division failure.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Use normal and zero-total fixtures.","grader_hint":"For a zero total, require a documented deterministic zero share rather than an exception or infinity."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A change is marked material when its absolute change is at least materiality_pct times prior exposure.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exercise below, exactly-at, and above-threshold fixtures.","grader_hint":"The exact threshold is inclusive."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"When prior exposure is zero, a non-zero current exposure is material and a zero current exposure is not material.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Run both zero-prior boundary cases.","grader_hint":"This tests the explicitly specified exception to percentage comparison."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The material_changes output contains exactly the obligor groups meeting the materiality rule and no others.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compare IDs or normalized names with an independent calculation.","grader_hint":"Do not award credit for merely exposing an internal boolean if the filtered list is wrong."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The concentration result identifies the largest confirmed operator concentration and reports its current share and exposure.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Independently calculate confirmed-group shares and compare.","grader_hint":"Use ±0.0001 for share and ±0.01 for exposure."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommendation is heightened committee review when the largest confirmed operator share is at least 0.30, and routine monitoring otherwise.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Run fixtures on both sides of and exactly at the 0.30 boundary.","grader_hint":"The 0.30 boundary is inclusive."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A source with duplicate certificate IDs raises ValueError rather than silently overwriting or aggregating duplicates.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Invoke the entry point with a duplicate-ID fixture.","grader_hint":"Only ValueError is acceptable for this contract violation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A syntactically parseable source with missing required fields, non-string text, an empty certificate list, or negative or non-finite exposures raises ValueError.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Invoke separate invalid semantic fixtures.","grader_hint":"The implementation must validate meaning, not merely JSON syntax."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A zero, negative, or greater-than-one materiality_pct raises ValueError, while a positive value no greater than one is accepted.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exercise all numeric-boundary cases.","grader_hint":"This must not be silently clamped or replaced by a default."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A non-real ISO date raises ValueError and a valid ISO date is echoed unchanged in the result.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Test malformed and calendar-invalid dates plus a valid date.","grader_hint":"Examples include 2024-02-30 and non-ISO strings."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All emitted obligor, certificate-ID, and material-change lists have deterministic ordering, and two runs on identical inputs are equal.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compare two return objects and inspect ordering.","grader_hint":"Do not rely on incidental dictionary or input order."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The implementation is understandable and safely reusable: assumptions, validation behavior, output schema, linkage interpretation, and reproduction steps are documented in one maintainer-facing place.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Review the code and README together.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a frontline analyst could adapt the model without reverse-engineering undocumented conventions."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Materiality and concentration thresholds are represented as clearly identifiable assumptions that a maintainer can change in one place or through the documented parameter, without editing duplicated business logic.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Inspect implementation structure and README.","grader_hint":"Do not award credit for scattered magic constants or duplicated threshold comparisons."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The package runs offline using Python 3.11 and the standard library alone, without network access, wall-clock dependence, or unseeded randomness.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Run in an offline clean environment and inspect imports and execution.","grader_hint":"The source JSON is the only factual input."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a reusable offline analytical model for a public-finance credit refresh. A frontline credit analyst will run it against the supplied certificate source and hand the resulting structured memo to a credit committee.","difficulty_sources":["Tracing an operator relationship across appropriation language and appendix disclosures rather than relying on issuer names","Aggregating current and prior-period exposures through several dependent transformations","Producing a deterministic, machine-readable memo contract that a credit-committee workflow can reuse"],"authoring_plan":{"source_file":{"filename":"certificate_holdings.json","construction":"Create one valid JSON object with a certificates array containing eleven synthetic records. Use unique certificate_id values, three synthetic state codes, and issuer values that differ across all or nearly all records. Include prior_exposure and current_exposure as non-negative finite numbers. Make exactly five records disclose the same operator name, Foxglove Clinic, with varied casing or spacing in at least one record; place that operator phrase in each of those five appropriation_text values. Include at least one other operator disclosure that appears only in operator_disclosure and not in appropriation_text, so the implementation must distinguish confirmed from unconfirmed linkage. Include Quarryfield Energy as an issuer value in at least one record. Make the five confirmed records span multiple issuer and state values and ensure their aggregate current share is at least 0.30 so the reference recommendation is heightened committee review. Give the dataset at least one material and one immaterial period change. Use no real identifiers or addresses."},"contract":{"entrypoint":"build_memo(source, as_of, materiality_pct=0.10)","input":"A parsed JSON object with a non-empty certificates list. Required record fields are certificate_id, issuer, state, prior_exposure, current_exposure, appropriation_text, and operator_disclosure.","output":"A JSON-serializable dictionary with as_of, total_prior_exposure, total_current_exposure, total_change, obligors, material_changes, concentration, and recommendation.","normalization":"Normalize operator disclosures and searchable appropriation text by Unicode case folding, trimming, and collapsing internal whitespace. Group on the normalized disclosure. Confirm a linkage when the normalized disclosure is found as a case-insensitive normalized substring in the corresponding appropriation text.","aggregation":"Sum prior and current exposures by normalized operator. Total portfolio values are sums over all records. Change is current minus prior. Current share is current group exposure divided by total current exposure, with zero for every share when the portfolio total is zero.","materiality":"For each group, material means abs(change) >= materiality_pct * prior when prior is positive; when prior is zero, material means current is non-zero. material_changes is the filtered group result.","concentration":"Among confirmed linked groups, select the greatest current share; tie-break by normalized operator name ascending. If no confirmed group exists, return a null concentration object and the routine recommendation. Heightened committee review applies at share >= 0.30.","validation":"Raise ValueError for wrong top-level shape, empty list, missing fields, duplicate IDs, invalid text types, negative or non-finite exposures, invalid ISO dates, and materiality_pct outside (0,1].","ordering":"Sort certificates within each group by certificate_id ascending; sort obligors and material_changes by normalized operator name ascending; use stable, explicit ordering for any evidence arrays."},"tests":["Check totals and group aggregation against an independent Decimal calculation.","Check five-record confirmed Foxglove Clinic linkage across different issuers.","Check issuer similarity and common wording do not create confirmation.","Check case and whitespace normalization.","Check materiality below, at, and above threshold.","Check zero-prior and zero-current boundary behavior.","Check 0.30 concentration boundary on both sides and at equality.","Check duplicate IDs, missing fields, wrong types, empty input, negative values, NaN, and infinity.","Check valid and invalid ISO dates.","Check deterministic ordering and equality across repeated runs.","Check output serialization with json.dumps.","Run offline in a clean Python 3.11 environment."],"documentation_requirements":["Document the public function signature and complete input/output schema.","Document validation exceptions and every business rule.","Document the linkage-evidence interpretation and limitations.","Provide a minimal offline invocation using certificate_holdings.json.","Keep thresholds and assumptions centralized and easy to change."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"certificate_holdings_source","filename":"certificate_holdings.json","purpose":"Complete synthetic source for the eleven lease-backed certificates, including prior and current exposures, issuer and state fields, appropriation language, and appendix operator disclosures.","required":true,"discovery":"Read this file from the working directory; it is the sole source of analytical facts."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"cross_holding_memo_package","filename":"cross_holding_obligor_memo.zip","media_type":"application/zip","description":"Offline Python 3.11 analytical model and maintainer documentation for producing the cross-holding obligor exposure memo.","required":true,"constraints":["The archive must contain cross_holding_obligor_memo.py and README.md.","The Python module must be executable and importable without network access or non-standard dependencies.","The documented public entry point and returned object must match the request exactly.","The implementation must not depend on wall-clock time, unseeded randomness, or hidden external data."],"rendering_required":false}],"work_activity":"analyze_data","work_product":"analytical_model","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"code_exec@v4","occupation":"financial_investment_analysts","sector":"finance_insurance","task_archetype":"code_exec","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"reference_script","reviewer_policy":"The build agent creates a reference implementation and executes the full contract test suite, including valid, invalid, boundary, determinism, and maintainability checks. A separate reviewer verifies that every tested convention is stated in the request and that the supplied source supports the intended linkage.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["The contract intentionally treats the supplied operator disclosure and appropriation text as the complete evidence universe; it does not perform external legal or credit research.","The memo recommendation is a deterministic screening recommendation, not a substitute for committee judgment."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:49:23+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:49:23+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:49:23+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:49:23+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['r09']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:49:23+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/4be553900db6f494","declared_deliverables":["cross_holding_obligor_memo.zip"]};
